title: Photosynthesis & Respiration
subject: Biology
level: GCSE
emoji: 🌱
description: How plants make food and how all organisms release energy.
---
Word equation for photosynthesis? :: Carbon dioxide + water → glucose + oxygen (in light, using chlorophyll).
Symbol equation for photosynthesis? :: 6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂
Is photosynthesis endothermic or exothermic? :: Endothermic – it takes in energy from light.
Where does photosynthesis happen? :: In chloroplasts, which contain chlorophyll.
Name three limiting factors of photosynthesis. :: Light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration and temperature.
How do plants use the glucose they make? :: Respiration, making starch/cellulose/fats/proteins, and storage.
Word equation for aerobic respiration? :: Glucose + oxygen → carbon dioxide + water (+ energy).
Symbol equation for aerobic respiration? :: C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂ → 6CO₂ + 6H₂O
Is respiration endothermic or exothermic? :: Exothermic – it releases energy.
Word equation for anaerobic respiration in muscles? :: Glucose → lactic acid (+ small amount of energy).
Word equation for anaerobic respiration in yeast? :: Glucose → ethanol + carbon dioxide (fermentation).
What is the oxygen debt? :: Extra oxygen needed after exercise to break down the lactic acid.
Which is more efficient: aerobic or anaerobic respiration? :: Aerobic respiration releases much more energy per glucose.
What do stomata do? :: Pores in the leaf that let gases in and out; opened and closed by guard cells.
What does xylem transport? :: Water and minerals from the roots up to the leaves.
What does phloem transport? :: Dissolved sugars (sucrose) around the plant – translocation.
What is transpiration? :: Evaporation of water from leaves, drawing more water up through the plant.
What test shows the presence of starch? :: Iodine solution turns from orange-brown to blue-black.
Why do plants need nitrates? :: To make amino acids and proteins.
Why do plants need magnesium? :: To make chlorophyll.
